(232143, 13304, 5475, '<td valign="top">Your subject matter here has the makings of a great photo, but your props really take away from that.  The baking pan and the red and white background and surface seem like an after thought for this photo.  If you can get some more of these, try this photo again with a nice cloth or other backdrop.  There is potential here for a great photo!  Good Luck,<br/>JD</td>', 'Your subject matter here has the makings of a great photo, but your props really take away from that.  The baking pan and the red and white background and surface seem like an after thought for this photo.  If you can get some more of these, try this photo again with a nice cloth or other backdrop.  There is potential here for a great photo!  Good Luck,JD', '2003-03-09 19:32:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(232153, 13306, 6870, '<td valign="top">In this image, the border looks like it''s encroaching on the image. This may be the photo that has been discussed for disqualification. I don''t think it should be, but you are certainly pushing the limits. the border does add to the nostalgic feel of the image, which is well lighted and well composed, but not significantly. I guess it would depend on the target audience. Remember that with this group, it would seem, most DPC members prefer good photos to good post-photo work. As for the photo itself, I really do love the light and shadows, and you captured a very nice candid moment with this lovely child. The sparkle in the eye is just right and needed. I would like to see whiter whites and darker darks, but I''m kinda weird that way. I love this shot.</td>', 'In this image, the border looks like it''s encroaching on the image. This may be the photo that has been discussed for disqualification. I don''t think it should be, but you are certainly pushing the limits. the border does add to the nostalgic feel of the image, which is well lighted and well composed, but not significantly. I guess it would depend on the target audience. Remember that with this group, it would seem, most DPC members prefer good photos to good post-photo work. As for the photo itself, I really do love the light and shadows, and you captured a very nice candid moment with this lovely child. The sparkle in the eye is just right and needed. I would like to see whiter whites and darker darks, but I''m kinda weird that way. I love this shot.', '2003-03-09 20:16:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(232155, 13481, 6870, '<td valign="top">Clear and messy: just right! My eye keeps wandering around this photo: it must be good! 10</td>', 'Clear and messy: just right! My eye keeps wandering around this photo: it must be good! 10', '2003-03-09 20:17:51.000000', NULL, 1),
