(233415, 13446, 4520, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jmsetzler:</b></div><hr/><i>Hmmm... lots of ones for this photo... unfortunately, those people don''t have the balls to stand up and tell you why they don''t like it... such is life... I expected to see this one rate a lot higher myself... It was one of the less ''mundane'' photos in this challenge... keep up the great work :) + fav</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for your comment and encouragement! :-) <br/>sorry I have a bad english, I''m limited!</td>', 'Originally posted by jmsetzler:Hmmm... lots of ones for this photo... unfortunately, those people don''t have the balls to stand up and tell you why they don''t like it... such is life... I expected to see this one rate a lot higher myself... It was one of the less ''mundane'' photos in this challenge... keep up the great work :) + fav  Thank you for your comment and encouragement! :-) sorry I have a bad english, I''m limited!', '2003-03-10 13:51:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(233455, 13513, 6855, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB<br/> <br/>Challenge: Met the challenge perfectly! <br/> <br/>Technique:  Very clever. Thanks for explaining how you did this!  Your lighting seems just a bit dark, but it still works.  I think your title is hilarious and very fitting.<br/> <br/>Settings:  Your settings appear right on.  Maybe a little post-challenge editing could smooth some of the noise on the egg and the bowl.  You may want to bump up your lighting, as this shot isn''t as "fresh" as it could be.<br/> <br/>Overall: A great shot!  I''m sorry you didn''t get the 6 you wanted, but there were so many great entries in this challenge!  I really like your originality in ALL your photos.</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB Challenge: Met the challenge perfectly!  Technique:  Very clever. Thanks for explaining how you did this!  Your lighting seems just a bit dark, but it still works.  I think your title is hilarious and very fitting. Settings:  Your settings appear right on.  Maybe a little post-challenge editing could smooth some of the noise on the egg and the bowl.  You may want to bump up your lighting, as this shot isn''t as "fresh" as it could be. Overall: A great shot!  I''m sorry you didn''t get the 6 you wanted, but there were so many great entries in this challenge!  I really like your originality in ALL your photos.', '2003-03-10 14:15:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(233464, 13518, 6855, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB<br/> <br/>Challenge:  Met the challenge perfectly, while still maintaining originality and creativity.<br/> <br/>Technique: Clever! This is really a gorgeous shot that should have scored a bit higher in my opinion.  It has a very "high-tech" look and feel to it.  I am curious how you got it to stand up on it''s own.<br/> <br/>Overall:  I really don''t see anything I would change here.  Your lighting and cropping are awesome, and nothing detracts from the image.  I apologize for the short critique, but this really is WELL DONE!</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB Challenge:  Met the challenge perfectly, while still maintaining originality and creativity. Technique: Clever! This is really a gorgeous shot that should have scored a bit higher in my opinion.  It has a very "high-tech" look and feel to it.  I am curious how you got it to stand up on it''s own. Overall:  I really don''t see anything I would change here.  Your lighting and cropping are awesome, and nothing detracts from the image.  I apologize for the short critique, but this really is WELL DONE!', '2003-03-10 14:18:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(233505, 13194, 6855, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB<br/> <br/>Challenge: Met the challenge perfectly, but a little too much focus is on the flower.<br/> <br/>Technique: Your lighting is awesome!  The colors are very warm and inviting, and the "off centered" approach makes it interesting to look at.  The reflection is great and very "clean"<br/> <br/>Overall: A GREAT shot!  I scored this one a 7 in the competition, and it is very well done.  Very original and fun to look at.</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB Challenge: Met the challenge perfectly, but a little too much focus is on the flower. Technique: Your lighting is awesome!  The colors are very warm and inviting, and the "off centered" approach makes it interesting to look at.  The reflection is great and very "clean" Overall: A GREAT shot!  I scored this one a 7 in the competition, and it is very well done.  Very original and fun to look at.', '2003-03-10 14:26:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(233655, 13306, 4494, '<td valign="top">Wow, I''m surprised this one didn''t do better.  I think people must have voted based on it being illegal.  I didn''t but it''s clear a lot of people did.<br/> <br/>Anyway good job, and congrats on it not being DQ''d.  I think if you would have left off the border you would have been MUCH higher in the ranking.</td>', 'Wow, I''m surprised this one didn''t do better.  I think people must have voted based on it being illegal.  I didn''t but it''s clear a lot of people did. Anyway good job, and congrats on it not being DQ''d.  I think if you would have left off the border you would have been MUCH higher in the ranking.', '2003-03-10 15:04:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(233757, 13282, 2716, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.  I really had fun with the background.  You''ll notice in my comments that the background is actually red ... I changed the colour with paint shop pro.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments.  I really had fun with the background.  You''ll notice in my comments that the background is actually red ... I changed the colour with paint shop pro.', '2003-03-10 15:55:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(233812, 13409, 6328, '<td valign="top">Critique Club by Silver Fox.<br/>This is an excellent Photo.  The background black is simple and pleasing to the eye and naturally does not take away from the main photograph of the bowl of flame.  You''ve done a good job of capturing the various colours of whites/yellows/red of temperaturs of the flames, but the problem is I can''t see the egg!<br/> <br/>Other than that, I''m at a real loss to tell you in what way you could possibly improve this photograph.  <br/> <br/>Is there any way you could possibly show the egg and not have as much flame?  I doubt it?  Can I possibly see an egg to the right of the small flame?  Is that it?<br/> <br/>Exposure/Lighting/Focus/Post Processing/ no issues what so ever<br/> <br/>Good jog - SharQ</td>', 'Critique Club by Silver Fox.This is an excellent Photo.  The background black is simple and pleasing to the eye and naturally does not take away from the main photograph of the bowl of flame.  You''ve done a good job of capturing the various colours of whites/yellows/red of temperaturs of the flames, but the problem is I can''t see the egg! Other than that, I''m at a real loss to tell you in what way you could possibly improve this photograph.   Is there any way you could possibly show the egg and not have as much flame?  I doubt it?  Can I possibly see an egg to the right of the small flame?  Is that it? Exposure/Lighting/Focus/Post Processing/ no issues what so ever Good jog - SharQ', '2003-03-10 16:26:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(233824, 13522, 3018, '<td valign="top">Felicidades Ceci! Qué bueno que metiste otra foto.  Esta me llamó la atención y me supuse (además de por el título) de que era de alguien de México.  Sigue participando!!!</td>', 'Felicidades Ceci! Qué bueno que metiste otra foto.  Esta me llamó la atención y me supuse (además de por el título) de que era de alguien de México.  Sigue participando!!!', '2003-03-10 16:39:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(233826, 13397, 3018, '<td valign="top">Ja! 200 fotos??? Así es con las fotos del dpchallenge.  Me gustó el ángulo con el que tomaste la foto.  Debiste haber ganado mejor calificación.  Felicidades por tu segunda foto, y no dejes de participar.</td>', 'Ja! 200 fotos??? Así es con las fotos del dpchallenge.  Me gustó el ángulo con el que tomaste la foto.  Debiste haber ganado mejor calificación.  Felicidades por tu segunda foto, y no dejes de participar.', '2003-03-10 16:42:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(233835, 13340, 6328, '<td valign="top">Critiqued by Silver Fox <br/>Sure hope it''s Hard Boiled :}<br/> <br/>Great Shot Doug!  My first thought was "Wow, really nice!"<br/> <br/>Composition is really nice, and I like the greens, browns, yellows of the grass that you''ve been able to capture on the ground.  It''s a nice sharp photo and the focus is great.<br/> <br/>I wonder if you could have shot it a bit lower though, and by doing so, you could have avoided the shadow of the egg on the golf club?  There is also a bit of a bluish/purple tone on the egg and the golf club, what''s that from?  By shooting lower, could it have been avoided?<br/> <br/>You met the challenge with your photo and I felt you had some Wow with this photo, surprised it came in so low, even if you were in the rough!</td>', 'Critiqued by Silver Fox Sure hope it''s Hard Boiled :} Great Shot Doug!  My first thought was "Wow, really nice!" Composition is really nice, and I like the greens, browns, yellows of the grass that you''ve been able to capture on the ground.  It''s a nice sharp photo and the focus is great. I wonder if you could have shot it a bit lower though, and by doing so, you could have avoided the shadow of the egg on the golf club?  There is also a bit of a bluish/purple tone on the egg and the golf club, what''s that from?  By shooting lower, could it have been avoided? You met the challenge with your photo and I felt you had some Wow with this photo, surprised it came in so low, even if you were in the rough!', '2003-03-10 16:45:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(233858, 13453, 6328, '<td valign="top">Critiqued by Silver Fox.<br/>Hello Geocide!<br/> <br/>It''s an interesting idea for the Challenge.<br/>I would assume that you''ve used two types of lighting here, one from the left and a blue one from the top? or is it just a blue tint done afterwards?<br/>The keyboard comes in nice and clear and focused but the Egg seems kind of fuzzy to my eyes.  Is that because of your image resizing?  And I like the way the background fades out to the darkness. . .<br/> <br/>The finishing score of 4.9 on your photo may be telling you something as I don''t really see anything technically wrong, so it must just be an issue of visual impact that held your score down, others did not see what you saw. . .  <br/> <br/>All in all, it''s nicely done, so keep trying!</td>', 'Critiqued by Silver Fox.Hello Geocide! It''s an interesting idea for the Challenge.I would assume that you''ve used two types of lighting here, one from the left and a blue one from the top? or is it just a blue tint done afterwards?The keyboard comes in nice and clear and focused but the Egg seems kind of fuzzy to my eyes.  Is that because of your image resizing?  And I like the way the background fades out to the darkness. . . The finishing score of 4.9 on your photo may be telling you something as I don''t really see anything technically wrong, so it must just be an issue of visual impact that held your score down, others did not see what you saw. . .   All in all, it''s nicely done, so keep trying!', '2003-03-10 17:00:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(233896, 13443, 6900, '<td valign="top">Hey all - thanks for the comments and votes.  I suppose my marks shall only go up.  I rushed this one, so I have skipped the Bridge Challenge and will probably submit to the From Above one.<br/> <br/>Yes, this was wax from a candle which I melted in a frying pan then poured onto paper as it was solidifying, then dumped the blue and white on it.  My idea was to have something strange coming from the drop - instead of a typical "dropped" egg shot.<br/> <br/>The ''blur'' was and wasn''t intentional.  It was in that if I didn''t do it at all, the wax was too clear - it looked LIKE WAX.  I wanted it to look a little fuzzier, but melting it and taking the picture wasn''t working - the sides were reflecting from the wetness.  So the intentional blur was there to try to soften what you saw and make it look like it came from the egg, not that I dropped an egg onto some wax.<br/> <br/>Thanks,<br/>Matt</td>', 'Hey all - thanks for the comments and votes.  I suppose my marks shall only go up.  I rushed this one, so I have skipped the Bridge Challenge and will probably submit to the From Above one. Yes, this was wax from a candle which I melted in a frying pan then poured onto paper as it was solidifying, then dumped the blue and white on it.  My idea was to have something strange coming from the drop - instead of a typical "dropped" egg shot. The ''blur'' was and wasn''t intentional.  It was in that if I didn''t do it at all, the wax was too clear - it looked LIKE WAX.  I wanted it to look a little fuzzier, but melting it and taking the picture wasn''t working - the sides were reflecting from the wetness.  So the intentional blur was there to try to soften what you saw and make it look like it came from the egg, not that I dropped an egg onto some wax. Thanks,Matt', '2003-03-10 17:21:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(234110, 13514, 4832, '<td valign="top">Great contrast! I love the metallic lines in the knife. <br/> <br/>The egg doesn''t look scared enough, though.</td>', 'Great contrast! I love the metallic lines in the knife.  The egg doesn''t look scared enough, though.', '2003-03-10 18:56:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(234234, 13421, 6855, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB<br/> <br/>Challenge: Definitely meets the challenge! You took a fun, creative approach.<br/> <br/>Technique:  I love the technique you used. The lighting is good, the cropping is excellent.  The texture of the egg adds interest while the crack adds a focal point.<br/> <br/>Suggestions: Lighting.  This is such a great shot, and it looks too dark.  Maybe spotlighting the crack a bit more would give you more of an effect?<br/> <br/>Overall: A great shot that should have scored a bit higher in my opinion.</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB Challenge: Definitely meets the challenge! You took a fun, creative approach. Technique:  I love the technique you used. The lighting is good, the cropping is excellent.  The texture of the egg adds interest while the crack adds a focal point. Suggestions: Lighting.  This is such a great shot, and it looks too dark.  Maybe spotlighting the crack a bit more would give you more of an effect? Overall: A great shot that should have scored a bit higher in my opinion.', '2003-03-10 20:12:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(234316, 13199, 5792, '<td valign="top">The egg challenge was very hard to judge this week. When there are so many good images to choose from some get short changed. This is one of them. There is no way this should have been rated below my entry that got a 5.2. One of my "top three" for the week "A Scrambled Egg" finished 140th.</td>', 'The egg challenge was very hard to judge this week. When there are so many good images to choose from some get short changed. This is one of them. There is no way this should have been rated below my entry that got a 5.2. One of my "top three" for the week "A Scrambled Egg" finished 140th.', '2003-03-10 21:11:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(234342, 13181, 5792, '<td valign="top">Not to take anything away from the winners, but I want everyone to know that I felt this was one of the three best images this week.</td>', 'Not to take anything away from the winners, but I want everyone to know that I felt this was one of the three best images this week.', '2003-03-10 21:28:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(234346, 13468, 5792, '<td valign="top">Not to take anything away from the winners, but I want everyone to know that I felt this was one of the three best images this week.<br/> <br/>The colors used (shell, scrambled egg and background) in this image are fantastic together! Composition and concept are top notch.</td>', 'Not to take anything away from the winners, but I want everyone to know that I felt this was one of the three best images this week. The colors used (shell, scrambled egg and background) in this image are fantastic together! Composition and concept are top notch.', '2003-03-10 21:32:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(234473, 13483, 6328, '<td valign="top">Hello Achiral.  Critique by Silver Fox.<br/> <br/>The colour and lighting are fine, although I tend to like to see a yellow egg yolk, not blue, but that''s just me.<br/> <br/>(While we''re on the lighting, I can spot a few reflections that I wonder if you could have taken care of, one at the bottom edge of the rim of the glass, lower right leading right up to the stem, also up towards the middle of the glass.)<br/> <br/>I think the perhaps you cropped a bit too tight?  It also looks like your table top is out of focus towards the back.<br/>Unfortunately you don''t give us any info on aperture/shutter, etc so we don''t know what you were up to.  <br/>I don''t know why you received such low scores because I don''t see anything technically wrong with your work, it''s just something that others didn''t seem to like, but you did meet the Challenge, so keep up the good work, and keep on "shooting".<br/>Ed<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello Achiral.  Critique by Silver Fox. The colour and lighting are fine, although I tend to like to see a yellow egg yolk, not blue, but that''s just me. (While we''re on the lighting, I can spot a few reflections that I wonder if you could have taken care of, one at the bottom edge of the rim of the glass, lower right leading right up to the stem, also up towards the middle of the glass.) I think the perhaps you cropped a bit too tight?  It also looks like your table top is out of focus towards the back.Unfortunately you don''t give us any info on aperture/shutter, etc so we don''t know what you were up to.  I don''t know why you received such low scores because I don''t see anything technically wrong with your work, it''s just something that others didn''t seem to like, but you did meet the Challenge, so keep up the good work, and keep on "shooting".Ed ', '2003-03-10 23:01:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(234683, 13418, 6536, '<td valign="top">Nice shot. Very funny.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by HBunch - Removed Critique Club status.</i></td>', 'Nice shot. Very funny.Message edited by HBunch - Removed Critique Club status.', '2003-03-11 08:24:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(234910, 13314, 1280, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Comments by Grayce<br/> <br/>This is cute!  Imaginative use of color too.  The composition is well done, with the eye drawn right to the subject...eggs.  I love the way you incorporated them.<br/>Exposure is fine, and your lighting is just right. The background is perfect for making the face stand out.<br/>There is no noise or digital artifacts, which is excellent.<br/>The time you took to set this up, and execute it paid off.  Terrific job!<br/>Regards,<br/> <br/>Grayce<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Comments by Grayce This is cute!  Imaginative use of color too.  The composition is well done, with the eye drawn right to the subject...eggs.  I love the way you incorporated them.Exposure is fine, and your lighting is just right. The background is perfect for making the face stand out.There is no noise or digital artifacts, which is excellent.The time you took to set this up, and execute it paid off.  Terrific job!Regards, Grayce', '2003-03-11 11:07:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(235157, 13394, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b>  Hello bjoggivik <br/>I''ll keep my critique short.<br/>I like this shot, daring and a cool idea.<br/>The lighting is really attractive.<br/>Like many of the comments below the _focus_. Of course this is a difficult shot to capture. Still I think this is a good attempt.</td>', 'CC  Hello bjoggivik I''ll keep my critique short.I like this shot, daring and a cool idea.The lighting is really attractive.Like many of the comments below the _focus_. Of course this is a difficult shot to capture. Still I think this is a good attempt.', '2003-03-11 16:18:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(235159, 13190, 6328, '<td valign="top">Critique by Silver Fox.<br/>Greetings.<br/> <br/>Great idea for the Challenge.  Your composition is nice.  I like the way you''ve captured the texture of the egg carton and the texture of the egg shells, but I think the color balance of the Egg Shells should have been a tad Whiter, and I really like the angle of the shot that you took.<br/> <br/>I believe though that the large black border takes away from your finished product as my eyes keep wandering from your eggs to the border all the time.<br/> <br/>I especially like the yellow of the egg and the egg white, but is there any way you could have avoided the reflections off of the egg whites, top and bottom and also from the next egg top?<br/> <br/>In regards to the Egg carton, where the egg white is flowing out of the carton - - it looks like the egg carton is cut into 2 pieces?  There is some shadow there also from one piece of the egg carton? where it does not meet the rest of the box properly?  What happened?<br/> <br/>Your use of cropping seems to be excellent.  DOF is fine.<br/> <br/>Your focus is okay, but the focus should have been more on the broken egg and then on the one behind it.  You''ve got the broken one slightly out of focus (on purpose?) and the one behind it in focus.  Were you concentrating more on the Egg Yolk instead of the broken shell?<br/> <br/>Nice photograph, Robbieh.<br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique by Silver Fox.Greetings. Great idea for the Challenge.  Your composition is nice.  I like the way you''ve captured the texture of the egg carton and the texture of the egg shells, but I think the color balance of the Egg Shells should have been a tad Whiter, and I really like the angle of the shot that you took. I believe though that the large black border takes away from your finished product as my eyes keep wandering from your eggs to the border all the time. I especially like the yellow of the egg and the egg white, but is there any way you could have avoided the reflections off of the egg whites, top and bottom and also from the next egg top? In regards to the Egg carton, where the egg white is flowing out of the carton - - it looks like the egg carton is cut into 2 pieces?  There is some shadow there also from one piece of the egg carton? where it does not meet the rest of the box properly?  What happened? Your use of cropping seems to be excellent.  DOF is fine. Your focus is okay, but the focus should have been more on the broken egg and then on the one behind it.  You''ve got the broken one slightly out of focus (on purpose?) and the one behind it in focus.  Were you concentrating more on the Egg Yolk instead of the broken shell? Nice photograph, Robbieh.  ', '2003-03-11 16:22:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(235162, 13320, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b>  Howdy cathysapp <br/>Fits The Challenge-Yes <br/>Composition-Like shaped fruit and an _egg_. <br/>Background-Stark <br/>My Opinion-I think the light is a bit harsh along with the white background. This photo would of been enhanced if a contrasting color had been used for the background. I lived a big part of life in the southern US, but this joke has escaped me! I do think the title is clever. Over all it''s a decent shot.</td>', 'CC  Howdy cathysapp Fits The Challenge-Yes Composition-Like shaped fruit and an _egg_. Background-Stark My Opinion-I think the light is a bit harsh along with the white background. This photo would of been enhanced if a contrasting color had been used for the background. I lived a big part of life in the southern US, but this joke has escaped me! I do think the title is clever. Over all it''s a decent shot.', '2003-03-11 16:25:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(235196, 13415, 6328, '<td valign="top">Critique by Silver Fox.<br/>Hello Nibularus.<br/> <br/>Well, you could still scramble it!  <br/> <br/>The colours are great, the yellow egg yolk and the white egg shell, even the pure egg whites, you''ve managed to capture them all. <br/> <br/>The lighting that you''ve used in this shot is very good, not overbearing at all, just one slight shadow from the one egg shell, and I had to really look to find it - excellent job on the lighting.<br/> <br/>Good focus, nice level that you took the shot from, good job!<br/>You''ve done a great job, congratulations.</td>', 'Critique by Silver Fox.Hello Nibularus. Well, you could still scramble it!   The colours are great, the yellow egg yolk and the white egg shell, even the pure egg whites, you''ve managed to capture them all.  The lighting that you''ve used in this shot is very good, not overbearing at all, just one slight shadow from the one egg shell, and I had to really look to find it - excellent job on the lighting. Good focus, nice level that you took the shot from, good job!You''ve done a great job, congratulations.', '2003-03-11 16:44:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(235332, 13514, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b>  Hey there jenarom <br/> <br/>Fits The Challenge- Yes,<br/>Composition- Neat. Really screams! Great fun title!<br/>Background- Plain, fitting for this black &amp; white shot.<br/>My Opinion- During the challenge I liked this shot and still do. It''s just got impact. I love the idea, the light and the shadow, the title.<br/>Good work.</td>', 'CC  Hey there jenarom  Fits The Challenge- Yes,Composition- Neat. Really screams! Great fun title!Background- Plain, fitting for this black & white shot.My Opinion- During the challenge I liked this shot and still do. It''s just got impact. I love the idea, the light and the shadow, the title.Good work.', '2003-03-11 19:09:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(235392, 13491, 1005, '<td valign="top">Oops I never saw the hair, honestly!  Where''s that cross and nails when you need it.  <br/>Nasty-gram backspaced!!!!<br/> <br/>How about this - if you don''t know a term, look it up!</td>', 'Oops I never saw the hair, honestly!  Where''s that cross and nails when you need it.  Nasty-gram backspaced!!!! How about this - if you don''t know a term, look it up!', '2003-03-11 19:51:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(235982, 13258, 6855, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB<br/> <br/>Challenge:  You met the challenge perfectly while still being very creative.<br/> <br/>Technique: Trying something new is always fun, and I''m glad you went out and tried this!  The yolk is very dark - in the future, simply put a "spotlight" on the yolk, or even a bright yellow circular piece of paper underneith it to make it show up better.  Really, that''s the only critisism you received here, but it''s an easy fix.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very clever and fun to look at.  I really like your approach, and I''m sorry you didn''t score a bit higher.  Keep trying! You are doing great and your creativity is really showing!</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB Challenge:  You met the challenge perfectly while still being very creative. Technique: Trying something new is always fun, and I''m glad you went out and tried this!  The yolk is very dark - in the future, simply put a "spotlight" on the yolk, or even a bright yellow circular piece of paper underneith it to make it show up better.  Really, that''s the only critisism you received here, but it''s an easy fix. Overall: Very clever and fun to look at.  I really like your approach, and I''m sorry you didn''t score a bit higher.  Keep trying! You are doing great and your creativity is really showing!', '2003-03-12 11:51:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(235983, 13445, 6855, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB<br/> <br/>Challenge: Met the challenge perfectly, while still being very creative and clever.<br/> <br/>Technique:  The only thing I would suggest here is to not use the on-camera flash. It adds alot of "wash" to the image and causes a large shadow behind the bird.  Simply by using high power lights, or even natural outdoor lighting (through a window), this image would have had much more depth and clarity.<br/> <br/>Overall:  A great idea that just needed some technical cleaning.</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB Challenge: Met the challenge perfectly, while still being very creative and clever. Technique:  The only thing I would suggest here is to not use the on-camera flash. It adds alot of "wash" to the image and causes a large shadow behind the bird.  Simply by using high power lights, or even natural outdoor lighting (through a window), this image would have had much more depth and clarity. Overall:  A great idea that just needed some technical cleaning.', '2003-03-12 11:53:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(235985, 13280, 6855, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB<br/> <br/>Challenge: Met the challenge perfectly, yet is still very creative. The title is very cute too.<br/> <br/>Technique:  The lighting is very intriguing, but some focus needed to be on the "plug" as alot of people didn''t know what this was.  I also think it would have looked great flipped upside down!  I really like the matching border, and the lighting is good, though a little dark.<br/> <br/>Overall:  A great photo, but it did have a little confusion with the lighting - again, simply by lighting the plug, I think you would have had better results.  VERY clever!  I know I wouldn''t have come up with something that cute!</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB Challenge: Met the challenge perfectly, yet is still very creative. The title is very cute too. Technique:  The lighting is very intriguing, but some focus needed to be on the "plug" as alot of people didn''t know what this was.  I also think it would have looked great flipped upside down!  I really like the matching border, and the lighting is good, though a little dark. Overall:  A great photo, but it did have a little confusion with the lighting - again, simply by lighting the plug, I think you would have had better results.  VERY clever!  I know I wouldn''t have come up with something that cute!', '2003-03-12 11:56:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(235986, 13289, 6855, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB<br/> <br/>Challenge:  You met the challenge perfectly while adding alot of color and depth!<br/> <br/>Technique:  Very creative and a good eye!  I like how the egg is off-centered, and the lighting you used is very good.  There is a slight tilt to the image that could be corrected simply by using a tripod.  The shadows add a lot of great effects as well.<br/> <br/>Overall:  A great photo that shows your creativity and eye for style.  There were so many great submissions in this challenge, so your score is commendable!  Great shot - not much here to really critique! =)</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB Challenge:  You met the challenge perfectly while adding alot of color and depth! Technique:  Very creative and a good eye!  I like how the egg is off-centered, and the lighting you used is very good.  There is a slight tilt to the image that could be corrected simply by using a tripod.  The shadows add a lot of great effects as well. Overall:  A great photo that shows your creativity and eye for style.  There were so many great submissions in this challenge, so your score is commendable!  Great shot - not much here to really critique! =)', '2003-03-12 11:58:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(235987, 13449, 6855, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB<br/> <br/>Challenge: Met the challenge perfectly, yet you still were very creative, adding alot of color and special "props"<br/> <br/>Technique: Cute, cute, cute.  This is a very fun pic to look at.  The colors are great! The lighting is a bit off, and the sprinkles from the peeps are a distraction, as well as where they were torn apart.  All of this could be fixed with some post-challenge editing.  There is also a little bit of tilt, that seems to always happen when taking a photo from above.  You might want to try resting your elbows on equal "planes" to keep your camera straight at this angle<br/> <br/>Overall: VERY CLEVER and so fun to look at! <br/></td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB Challenge: Met the challenge perfectly, yet you still were very creative, adding alot of color and special "props" Technique: Cute, cute, cute.  This is a very fun pic to look at.  The colors are great! The lighting is a bit off, and the sprinkles from the peeps are a distraction, as well as where they were torn apart.  All of this could be fixed with some post-challenge editing.  There is also a little bit of tilt, that seems to always happen when taking a photo from above.  You might want to try resting your elbows on equal "planes" to keep your camera straight at this angle Overall: VERY CLEVER and so fun to look at! ', '2003-03-12 12:01:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(236091, 13294, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b>  Hello ziggy<br/> <br/>Fits The Challenge-YES <br/>Composition-Very nice, interesting. <br/>Background-N/A <br/>My Opinion-I think the crop in combination with the frame hurt this shot. Was there a reason you did it like this? I do think the lighting added to the shot and made it appealing. The water is.....sweat? Just a guess, but I like it. Good job.<br/> <br/></td>', 'CC  Hello ziggy Fits The Challenge-YES Composition-Very nice, interesting. Background-N/A My Opinion-I think the crop in combination with the frame hurt this shot. Was there a reason you did it like this? I do think the lighting added to the shot and made it appealing. The water is.....sweat? Just a guess, but I like it. Good job. ', '2003-03-12 14:51:07.000000', NULL, 0),
