(237289, 13380, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>COMPOSITION<br/>The composition of this is awesome.  The shape of the hand really draws the eyes down to the egg.  Also, the bracelet, to me, helps to anchor the picture, or give the eyes somewhere to start.  Nice addition.  Like others have mentioned, if you could have flipped this so that the egg looked "balanced" on you finger.<br/> <br/>TECHNIQUE<br/>The focus here works well, and I think the "muted" gray look really helps the egg stand out.  Color might have been okay, if the background was a soft gray or brown, otherwise, i think the bw makes it effective.  A little light from the right may have helped it some (for some viewers) but I like the soft lighting predominately on one side.<br/> <br/>OVERALL EFFECT<br/>This was a great idea, and a good approach to the challenge.  I am really surprised it didn''t score higher, as it is a high quality picture.  Sorry I can''t offer more suggestions as to how to improve it.<br/> <br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat COMPOSITIONThe composition of this is awesome.  The shape of the hand really draws the eyes down to the egg.  Also, the bracelet, to me, helps to anchor the picture, or give the eyes somewhere to start.  Nice addition.  Like others have mentioned, if you could have flipped this so that the egg looked "balanced" on you finger. TECHNIQUEThe focus here works well, and I think the "muted" gray look really helps the egg stand out.  Color might have been okay, if the background was a soft gray or brown, otherwise, i think the bw makes it effective.  A little light from the right may have helped it some (for some viewers) but I like the soft lighting predominately on one side. OVERALL EFFECTThis was a great idea, and a good approach to the challenge.  I am really surprised it didn''t score higher, as it is a high quality picture.  Sorry I can''t offer more suggestions as to how to improve it. karmat', '2003-03-14 12:32:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(237291, 13261, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>COMPOSITION<br/>I like the overall composition of this.  The curve of the plate, with the eggs following it, allow the eyes to travel in a graceful path from one side of the picture to the other.  I also think the negative space in the upper part of the picture helps to make the focus on the eggs.  It seems a little tight on the right, though.  I would recommend a tighter crop on the right or bottom, or allowing more space on the right to give it a more balanced feeling.<br/> <br/>TECHNIQUE<br/>The focus in this shot is good, and I think it is lit well.  It is bright enough to see the details, but not too bright so that the white spots are blown out.  The reflection of the eggs add a nice touch.<br/> <br/>OVERALL EFFECT<br/>Great work at meeting the challenge.  Looks like maybe you should have boiled the eggs just a touch longer! &lt;vbg&gt; :-)<br/> <br/>best to you in future challenges.<br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat COMPOSITIONI like the overall composition of this.  The curve of the plate, with the eggs following it, allow the eyes to travel in a graceful path from one side of the picture to the other.  I also think the negative space in the upper part of the picture helps to make the focus on the eggs.  It seems a little tight on the right, though.  I would recommend a tighter crop on the right or bottom, or allowing more space on the right to give it a more balanced feeling. TECHNIQUEThe focus in this shot is good, and I think it is lit well.  It is bright enough to see the details, but not too bright so that the white spots are blown out.  The reflection of the eggs add a nice touch. OVERALL EFFECTGreat work at meeting the challenge.  Looks like maybe you should have boiled the eggs just a touch longer! <vbg> :-) best to you in future challenges.karmat', '2003-03-14 12:41:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(237297, 13353, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Congrats on your first entry!<br/> <br/>COMPOSITION<br/>I like the overall composition of this.  It has a solid anchored feeling by placing the "egg" in the lower right hand corner, and gives the eye something to rest upon.  It seems to be cropped a bit tight on the right and bottom, so I would recommend giving yourself a little more space on those two sides, just to give a little more room.<br/> <br/>TECHNIQUE<br/>Generally, (and unfortunately) pictures with soft focus historically do not do well for dpc.  I do think, however, this shot would have been more effective with a sharp clear focus.  Reading your comment below, I think you did the right thing by having the outer edge, and not the center, soft.  It also seems a bit dark, to me.  I would suggest using a tripod and slowing the shutter down to allow more light.  Or lighting the candle!<br/> <br/>OVERALL EFFECT<br/>A great idea.  You have met the challenge well, and in a creative fashion.  Best to you in the future challenges.  Have fun!!<br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Congrats on your first entry! COMPOSITIONI like the overall composition of this.  It has a solid anchored feeling by placing the "egg" in the lower right hand corner, and gives the eye something to rest upon.  It seems to be cropped a bit tight on the right and bottom, so I would recommend giving yourself a little more space on those two sides, just to give a little more room. TECHNIQUEGenerally, (and unfortunately) pictures with soft focus historically do not do well for dpc.  I do think, however, this shot would have been more effective with a sharp clear focus.  Reading your comment below, I think you did the right thing by having the outer edge, and not the center, soft.  It also seems a bit dark, to me.  I would suggest using a tripod and slowing the shutter down to allow more light.  Or lighting the candle! OVERALL EFFECTA great idea.  You have met the challenge well, and in a creative fashion.  Best to you in the future challenges.  Have fun!!karmat', '2003-03-14 12:59:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(237595, 13446, 6328, '<td valign="top">Greetings Lili,<br/>Critique by Silver Fox.<br/> <br/>Lovely Black and White Photography.<br/>I love this.  Your egg is nice and white, but I can''t hear your human laying the egg, my sound is not turned up high enough :} (my sense of humor)<br/>I really like your lighting, and the posing of your human is absolutely terrific, the arms and hands are perfect and the open mouth I think is excellent.  How many eggs does he lay on an average day? :} my humor again. . .<br/>I cannot find anything technically wrong with your photograph!<br/> <br/>This is a very creative, and in my humble thinking, an elegant image for this competition/challenge.  The positioning of the egg and the model were excellent choices and make the shot what it is. . .<br/> <br/>Lighting: the lighting creates the image and you made a good choice in choosing the black cloth as a background.  There is a bit of sharp light reflection off the right elbow, that can''t really be helped.<br/> <br/>Camera: Good focus, Nice sharp image throughout.<br/> <br/>Digital Processing.  I believe that you made the egg whiter in the processing and good for you, it looks great and stands out well.<br/> <br/>My opionion: Great job, great imagination for a difficult Challenge. <br/> <br/> I liked the creativity that you came up with and you deserve the Congratulations of a job well done.<br/>Finally: I don''t understand why you scored so low, and I''m going to say only that people just don''t appreciate fine art and can''t laugh at  themsselves any more, so ignore them and just keep shooting the good works that you are capable of doing. . .<br/>Regards,<br/>Ed</td>', 'Greetings Lili,Critique by Silver Fox. Lovely Black and White Photography.I love this.  Your egg is nice and white, but I can''t hear your human laying the egg, my sound is not turned up high enough :} (my sense of humor)I really like your lighting, and the posing of your human is absolutely terrific, the arms and hands are perfect and the open mouth I think is excellent.  How many eggs does he lay on an average day? :} my humor again. . .I cannot find anything technically wrong with your photograph! This is a very creative, and in my humble thinking, an elegant image for this competition/challenge.  The positioning of the egg and the model were excellent choices and make the shot what it is. . . Lighting: the lighting creates the image and you made a good choice in choosing the black cloth as a background.  There is a bit of sharp light reflection off the right elbow, that can''t really be helped. Camera: Good focus, Nice sharp image throughout. Digital Processing.  I believe that you made the egg whiter in the processing and good for you, it looks great and stands out well. My opionion: Great job, great imagination for a difficult Challenge.   I liked the creativity that you came up with and you deserve the Congratulations of a job well done.Finally: I don''t understand why you scored so low, and I''m going to say only that people just don''t appreciate fine art and can''t laugh at  themsselves any more, so ignore them and just keep shooting the good works that you are capable of doing. . .Regards,Ed', '2003-03-15 05:07:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(237596, 13399, 6328, '<td valign="top">Critique by Silver Fox<br/> <br/>Nice overall depth of field on the eggs and the egg carton but a more shallow depth of field may have been better used in this photograph.<br/> <br/>Great idea to choose brown eggs instead of white, but you made them just slightly too brown.  The texture in the first eggshell seems okay<br/>but the rest of the are blurred so you can''t tell.<br/> <br/>The table and light just behond the egg carton are very distracting, moves your subjects eyes away from your main focus almost immediately.<br/> <br/>Would like to have seen sharper focus on the first two eggs and the first two or three humps of the carton.<br/> <br/>You had a great idea and show lots of imagination for the challenge.<br/>I also like the way you use the rule of 3rds here.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique by Silver Fox Nice overall depth of field on the eggs and the egg carton but a more shallow depth of field may have been better used in this photograph. Great idea to choose brown eggs instead of white, but you made them just slightly too brown.  The texture in the first eggshell seems okaybut the rest of the are blurred so you can''t tell. The table and light just behond the egg carton are very distracting, moves your subjects eyes away from your main focus almost immediately. Would like to have seen sharper focus on the first two eggs and the first two or three humps of the carton. You had a great idea and show lots of imagination for the challenge.I also like the way you use the rule of 3rds here. ', '2003-03-15 05:23:15.000000', NULL, 0),
